	(text "LAYOUT (section 8.5): TP8 on KA_N2 keeps ground around it. No pad on KA_N1.\nKeep this pump (R29, C22, D7) at least 10 mm from the relay pump (R89, C51, D22)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0312cb18-bd87-5ac5-8855-71084b15eabe")
	)
	(text "Over-current window comparator on ISENSE_LO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.67 142.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0c444da9-0253-5af3-943e-3ca2c380055f")
	)
	(text "FAIL-SAFE GATE (hardware design section 8) and OVER-CURRENT LATCH (section 9).\n\nDetector A. Firmware toggles KA (GPIO17) every 5 ms. It needs an edge at least every 20 ms\nand no phase shorter than 2.5 ms (the second is for detector B on the expander sheet).\nEach rising edge pushes charge through C22 and D7 into C23. R30 and R91 (two, so that one open\nresistor only doubles the hold-up) drain it. U6A switches on at 1.55 V on KA_N2 and off at 0.94 V\n(R31, R32 hysteresis; reference 1.32 V from R34, R35). With 5 ms edges V_DRV is on 13 to 22 ms\nafter the first edge and off 0.21 to 0.83 s after the last, 1.25 s if the pin stops high\n(simulated corners of review A2). A steady level, high or low, never enables it.\nR33 holds KA low while the ESP32 is in reset. It is 2.2k so that a net behind a 10k pull-up\ncannot run the detectors through a solder bridge.\n\nDRV_EN = KA_OK AND NOT FAULT. Low does three things: Q3 removes V_DRV from every opto LED, the\nexpander is held in reset, and the expander bit that drives relay transistor Q1 is released.\nV_DRV_RB (through R92) is V_DRV, behind Q3, read on GPIO42: firmware times detector A with it\nand sees a shorted Q3 as drive that is on with no keep-alive.\n\nOver-current. U6B pulls OC_TRIP_N low above VH (1.425 V), U6C below VL (0.188 V): 4.6 A peak in\neither polarity, 4.0 to 5.4 A over tolerance, about 70 us after a short begins (R52, C33: 47 us).\nU7A and U7B latch it. D8 lights while FAULT is set. Only KA_OK going low clears the latch.\nR87 stops GPIO40 from overdriving the latch node if it is ever left as an output.\n\nU7 is a 74HC132: Schmitt inputs for the slow edges of the open-collector comparators.\n\n3V3 over-voltage (section 9.5). If U3 shorts, 3V3 goes to V5 and the ESP32 is outside its\nratings. U13 pulls OC_TRIP_N low while 3V3 is above 4.04 V (3.91 to 4.17 V): DRV_EN is then\nlow whatever KA does, and D8 is lit. C55 with the divider is 1 ms. U13 can only remove drive."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.86 210.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2e69992e-5e4a-5ccc-98bb-6c6aed3867f2")
	)
	(text "Latch and drive enable"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 265.43 127.66 0)
		(effects
